' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Simple UML-RT/ROOM: one capsule with two typed ports and a protocol with in/out signals.
'   usecase:      Teach capsule, port, protocol (in/out signals), and connector.
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       rose-realtime / uml-rt
' ============================================================================
title Example Rose RealTime - Simple Capsule

' UML-RT (ROOM) core concepts:
'   Capsule  - active, concurrent executable unit (modeled as a class w/ <<capsule>>)
'   Port     - typed by a Protocol; a communication endpoint on the capsule boundary
'   Protocol - defines IN signals (received) and OUT signals (sent)
'   Connector- wires two ports of compatible protocols together

' ---- Protocol: SensorProtocol ----
class "SensorProtocol\n<<protocol>>" as P1 {
  + in: readRequest()
  + out: sample(data)
}

' ---- Capsule: SensorReader ----
class "SensorReader\n<<capsule>>" as CAP1 {
  behavior: state machine
}

' Two ports on the capsule boundary, typed by the protocol.
' (relay ports pass through; external end connects to a peer.)
rectangle "p1: SensorProtocol" as PT1
rectangle "p2: SensorProtocol" as PT2

CAP1 --> PT1 : "port"
CAP1 --> PT2 : "port"

PT1 --> P1 : "typed by"
PT2 --> P1 : "typed by"

note bottom of CAP1
  Ports carry SIGNALS governed by the Protocol.
  The capsule has an executable state machine reacting to in-signals
  and emitting out-signals.
end note
